<!-- A layout wraps every page below it in the route tree. It renders its child page through `<slot/>` —
     the same outlet a component uses, filled by the router instead of by a caller's `<Tag>…</Tag>`, so
     there is nothing layout-specific to learn.

     A layout SURVIVES a soft navigation: a cross-route nav that shares a layout prefix keeps the shared
     outer layouts mounted and swaps only the diverging suffix. So state you put in a `<script>` here
     outlives navigation, and an effect here does not re-run per page. -->
<main class="app">
  <slot/>
</main>

<style>
  .app { max-width: 42rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
</style>
